  {
   "what": "C-KN: the 1x fund (KODEX 200) night/day series has no data from 2007-02-08 to 2009-04-17. \"2007-2014\" is really 7 days of early 2007 plus 2009-04-20 onward (1,425 rows; 2008 has none, 2007 has 7). The sealed text describes the series as 2007-01-30..2014-12-30 and \"8 years available\".",
   "severity": "medium (description of the test, not the verdict)",
   "evidence": "k_n rows per year: {\"2007\": 7, \"2009\": 179, \"2010\": 251, \"2011\": 248, \"2012\": 248, \"2013\": 247, \"2014\": 245}. G1 on 2009-04-20 onward only: t = 4.46 (n = 1418), so the pass of G1 does not depend on the 7 rows of 2007, but the 2008 crash is absent from G1, G2 and G3. G3 has 7 years, not 8: 5 positive of 7 (2007 is 7 nights). Fails \"6 of 8\" as sealed, fails 6 of 7 if rescaled, and is 4 of 6 without the 7-night year."
  },
  {
   "what": "C-KN: annual growth of the synthetic series is spread over the 7.92 calendar years between first and last row although only about 5.77 years of trading days exist. This understates every per-year figure of the synthetic series (night-only and buy-and-hold alike).",
   "severity": "low (no gate changes)",
   "evidence": "synthetic night-only at 0.046%: 0.1542 per year on the calendar span (sealed convention, matches yours) versus 0.2174 per 247 trading days; buy-and-hold 0.0757 versus 0.1053; at 0.092%: 0.0625 versus 0.0867. The synthetic leg of G2 passes either way; G2 fails on the actual 2x fund (0.0102 < 0.08)."
  },
  {
   "what": "C-KN: G1 passes only on the 1x fund series, which the tradable products contradict. On the common sample the 1x fund shows about twice the night return of the actual 2x fund (per unit of exposure), and the night-minus-day t-statistic drops below 3 on every tradable series.",
   "severity": "medium (G1 = true is correct as sealed, but it should not be quoted as evidence of a tradable effect)",
   "evidence": "common sample n = 1204: mean night bp 1x fund 5.61 vs half of 2x fund 2.98 vs minus inverse fund 2.19; difference 1x - half 2x = 2.63 bp per night (NW t = 4.47). Night-minus-day NW t: 1x fund 3.83, actual 2x fund 2.05, futures proxy 1.77, minus inverse 1.30. Close-to-close means agree far better (1x 1.64 bp, half 2x 1.25 bp), so the gap is in where the open price sits, not in the total return. Largest negative gaps fall on late-April dates (fund distribution dates), as the sealed text expected, but they are outweighed on the other days."
  },
